# A getter, a setter and a method are written in a literal (L1) that is handed out, so nothing is proven of their `this`. By their own text it is an object created below the literal, where one is created: L2, made by Object.create two steps below.
# It is an expectation with its test, as `this` of a method of a class: the entry is guarded and the accesses are typed.
# RUN: link functions mechanisms=all
# CHECK: function f2 cycle
# CHECK-NEXT: parameter 0 expected=L2 declared
# CHECK: function f3 cycle
# CHECK-NEXT: parameter 0 expected=L2 declared
# CHECK: function f4 cycle
# CHECK-NEXT: parameter 0 expected=L2 declared
# RUN(GETTER): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# GETTER: b0(v0: L2?ParameterOfEscapedFunction
# GETTER: = GetSlotOrUndefined v0 {{*}}key="_body" receivers=[L2] level=Expected
# RUN(SETTER): walk f3 mechanisms=all
# SETTER: = PutSlotOrAdd v0, v1 {{*}}key="_body" receivers=[L2] level=Expected
# -- source: this-of-a-member-written-in-a-literal-is-expected-to-be-of-the-literal-or-created-below-it.js
